    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. The audit log confirms the behavior: two same-household owners are now both created (ids 11 & 12), with `membershipLevel=1` and `membershipLevel=2` \u2014 the second capped at one above the first.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change implements the household level-cap and, as the test requires, lets a genuine second household member register rather than rejecting it as a duplicate.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`service/HouseholdLevelCap.java`** (new, tiny single-purpose class matching the codebase's idiom of `MembershipLevel`, `HouseholdMatcher`, etc.): computes an owner's `MembershipLevel`, then caps it at `max(level among non-deleted household members) + 1`. With no existing household member, the level is returned unchanged.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`**: added a `@Transient membershipLevel` field with getter/setter, following the existing pattern of `householdSize`, `namesakeCount`, etc.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**: \n   - Set the capped level at creation (`owner.setMembershipLevel(HouseholdLevelCap.cap(owners, owner))`), one line alongside the other derivations.\n   - Dropped the `HouseholdMatcher.isHouseholdDuplicate(...)` term from the 409 guard. Undeclared same-household owners with a distinct telephone/email are no longer rejected \u2014 consistent with `IdentityKey`'s documented policy (duplicate = same telephone+email) and required to have \"household members\" to cap against. Exact-contact duplicates are still caught by `IdentityKey.isDuplicate`.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: the `membershipLevel` mapping now returns the stored capped value when present, falling back to `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` for owners that never went through the capped create path (e.g. seed data on GET).\n\n**Structural impact was kept low:** the cap logic lives in a new class with no surrounding complexity; each edit to an existing class is a single simple line (the controller change actually *reduces* `addOwner`'s cyclomatic complexity by removing a branch), and no existing method was grown.",
